Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 15:13:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(web): pair LAN mobile browsers with a six-digit PIN

`dsh web --host 0.0.0.0` now serves a pairing page to mobile browsers on the
local network, so the Web GUI opens from a phone without putting the opaque
launch token in the mobile URL. The page trades a process-local six-digit PIN
for the same authority-bound browser cookie the local launch URL already uses,
and locks a peer address out after repeated failed submissions.

The built-bin acceptance case that asserted the removed usage error now covers
the surviving `--port` usage error, and the assembled Web snapshot asserts the
clean LAN URL and PIN line.
